            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "A pretty good working solution for this I found was to have a pre write hook that dismisses all notifications like so:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal minisessions = require(\"mini.sessions\")\r\nminisessions.setup({\r\n    hooks = {\r\n        pre = {\r\n            write = function()\r\n                vim.notify.dismiss({ silent = true, pending = true })\r\n            end,\r\n        },\r\n    },\r\n    verbose = { read = true, write = true, delete = true, },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nI could probably find some way to close all buffers that are creating problems for me through this hook. Feel free to close this issue if this solution is satisfactory for most people.\r\n\r\nThanks",
