            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I wanted to have a session that is always what I was working on last.\r\n\r\nSo like a backup session? Nice.\r\n\r\n> A pretty good working solution for this I found was to have a pre write hook that dismisses all notifications like so:\r\n\r\nDouble nice! It is actually a first time someone used this plugin in a way I didn't anticipate beforehand. Kudos!\r\n\r\nTo make it work with all \"special buffers\", take a look at `buftype` option. Usually those special buffers have its value set to `nofile`. So making a custom cleanup function using `vim.api.nvim_list_bufs()` can do the trick.\r\n\r\nWon't close issue for a bit to ponder about deciding whether to put this kind of cleanup in plugin or leave as help/wiki entry.",
