            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for the tip! What I was doing before was quite... not great 🤣 \r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal close_bad_buffers = function()\r\n  local buffer_infos = vim.split(vim.api.nvim_exec(\"buffers!\", true), \"\\n\")\r\n  local bad_buffers = { \"NvimTree\", \"Neogit\", \"packer\" }\r\n  for _, buffer_info in pairs(buffer_infos) do\r\n      local buffer_id = vim.split(buffer_info, \"%s\", { trimempty = true })[1]:match(\"%d+\")\r\n      local _, buffer_name, _ = buffer_info:match('(\")(.+)(\")')\r\n      for _, bad_buffer in pairs(bad_buffers) do\r\n          if string.find(buffer_name, bad_buffer) then\r\n              pcall(vim.cmd, \"bd \" .. buffer_id)\r\n              break\r\n          end\r\n      end\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nI appreciate it a lot as I'm quite new to diving into Neovim (evidently above). Honestly, your plugins have been such a great way to get acquainted into the Neovim ecosystem. Thank you so much for that.",
